# STEP 2 of 2 — layer the official sampling parameters onto the imported model.
#
# Values are copied verbatim from the Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B-Instruct model card,
# "Best Practices" section:
#     temperature=0.7, top_p=0.8, top_k=20, repetition_penalty=1.05
# The card recommends an output length of 65536 for most queries; 8192 is plenty
# for chat replies and keeps responses snappy.
#
#   ollama create qwen3-coder:30b -f models/Modelfile.qwen3-coder-30b-tuned
#   ollama show qwen3-coder:30b --parameters      # must list all five
#
# This reuses the existing blob - it does NOT copy the 17 GB of weights again
# (the create log says "using existing layer sha256:...").
#
# Deliberately NOT set here:
#   num_ctx  - would override the global OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH (see README)
#   TEMPLATE - would override Ollama's built-in qwen3-coder renderer; the working
#              chat + tool-call template comes from the GGUF itself
#
# Side effect worth knowing: re-creating a tag makes Ollama swap the runner, and
# one or two requests can fail with HTTP 400 in that window. Retry once.
FROM qwen3-coder:30b
PARAMETER temperature 0.7
PARAMETER top_p 0.8
PARAMETER top_k 20
PARAMETER repeat_penalty 1.05
PARAMETER num_predict 8192
